    m_HorizontalOverflow: 0
    m_VerticalOverflow: 0
    m_LineSpacing: 1
  m_Text: 'The first dinosaurs walked the earth around two hundred million years ago.
    The Cambrian would occur three hundred million years before these giants walked
    the earth.


    But all the dinosaurs, and in fact everything that existed on earth after the
    Cambrian, would owe their appearance and behaviour to the struggles and successes
    of organisms that lived and died during the Cambrian.'
